== specs/system-speckit/042-decision-capture/scratch/runs/w2-writer/
  export function recordConsumedKeys(projectRoot: string, packet: string, ids: Array<{ sourceKey: string; id: string }>, now: string): void

RULES for writeDecisionRecord(folder, entries):
1. A sourceKey must match /^[A-Za-z0-9:._-]+$/ or throw BAD_SOURCE_KEY before writing anything. A repeated sourceKey in one call is ignored after its first entry.
2. recordPath = path.join(folder, 'decision-record.md'). The doc has two anchored sections. Section A: `<!-- ANCHOR:operator-decisions -->`, `## Operator Decisions`, blank, `| ID | Decided | Why | Supersedes | Carried by |`, `|----|---------|-----|------------|------------|`, rows, `<!-- /ANCHOR:operator-decisions -->`. Section B: `<!-- ANCHOR:operator-answers-verbatim -->`, `## Appendix: Verbatim Operator Answers`, blank, `Each appendix item uses the same id as its operator decision. The options are included so the record preserves the full offered choice set.`, items, `<!-- /ANCHOR:operator-answers-verbatim -->`. When the file exists but a section is missing, append that section at the end after a blank line, `---`, blank line.
