== specs/system-speckit/042-decision-capture/scratch/runs/w4-sweep/
1. session_id = the first line's sessionId, else the transcript file name without .jsonl.
2. Tool answers: remember every assistant tool_use with name 'AskUserQuestion' by id. For each tool result line whose tool_result.tool_use_id is remembered and whose toolUseResult.answers is an object, call normalizeAskUserQuestion({ runtime:'claude', sessionId: session_id, toolUseId: tool_use_id, toolInput: the remembered input, toolResponse: toolUseResult, source:'transcript', now }). Append all records with appendRecords(projectDir, session_id, records); recovered = its appended count.
3. pending = pendingRecords(projectDir, session_id).
4. Chat candidates: keep lastText = { uuid, text } from the most recent assistant line that has text blocks (text blocks joined with '\n'); set lastText = null on any assistant line that has a tool_use block, because a later tool call means that text did not close the turn. On a typed user prompt line: if lastText is set, take the last non-empty paragraph of lastText.text (paragraphs split on blank lines); if it contains '?', it is a candidate with question = that paragraph byte-exact, answer = the typed text byte-exact, question_turn_id = lastText.uuid, answer_turn_id = the user line uuid, key = chatSourceKey('claude', session_id, question_turn_id, answer_turn_id). Then set lastText = null. At the end of the file, a still-set lastText whose last paragraph contains '?' is a candidate with answer null, answer_turn_id null and key null.
5. Drop a candidate when isProcessQuestion({ question, header:'', options }) is true, where options = the paragraph's lines that match /^\s*(?:[-*]\s+)?(?:\*\*)?[A-D]\)/ with leading bullet and ** markers removed. Drop a candidate whose key is in readConsumedKeys(projectDir).
